  // confirmed — the record holds customer PII and should not outlive the request that
  // needs it. It is React memory only (never storage, never logged) and dies on unmount.
```

Most of Option 3 was already in the file when I went to apply it — you'd landed it from the diff. I added the PII-reset note I'd promised and verified the whole thing.

## Verification

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| `tsc --noEmit` | ✅ 0 errors |
| `eslint` (footer) | ✅ **0 errors, 0 warnings** — was 2 |
| `prettier --check` (footer) | ✅ clean |
| `vitest run` | ✅ 164 passed / 5 files |
| Repo-wide warnings | **5 → 3** |

The 3 remaining warnings are all `header/index.tsx:41,45,64` — the orphan imports feeding the commented-out JSX block from item 8, which AGENTS.md prevents us from removing. Nothing new.

The 19 `prettier/prettier` errors in `contentful/experiences/definitions.ts` and `routes.tsx` are untouched and identical to `develop` — pre-existing, and no workflow runs `npm run lint` anyway.

## Still open on #12

**12c — the stale `ContactIconRow` header comment.** `index.tsx:262-264` still says the icons render as `<span aria-hidden>` and are *"excluded from the tab order and from assistive tech announcements"* — which our own last fix made false. The correct rationale sits 25 lines below it in the fallback branch, so the file currently argues both ways.

That's a one-comment change with no code impact. Want me to do it, or hold it with #11?

