input.new_string:
// Figma: flex-col, gap-16px, 140px wide on mobile; content-sized on tablet+ but CAPPED.
//
// The cap reproduces a per-item constraint in the design: Figma's "ACKNOWLEDGEMENT OF
// COUNTRY" item (40000407:11004) is 118x38 — constrained to the width of its longest
// word so it wraps onto two lines. Every other footer nav label in the design is
// <=135px and stays on one line, so capping the column at SIZE_COL_NAV (140px) forces
// that one label to wrap and leaves the rest untouched. Without it the About column
// renders ~212px wide, which pushes the space-between distribution off spec (Contact
// lands 34px right of Figma; with the cap, 4px).
//
// Exact column widths still will not match Figma (About 140 vs 118, Help 120 vs 106):
// those are content-driven and the fallback font renders ~13% wider than Futura Round,
// which cannot be self-hosted under the Monotype licence. Not a build defect.
// Pending Kiera: confirm the cap is the right rule vs a per-item wrap.
linkCol: {
  display: 'flex',
  flexDirection: 'column',
  gap: 'm',
  alignItems: 'flex-start',
  width: SIZE_COL_NAV,
  minWidth: 0,
  flexShrink: 0,
