content.text:
Everything confirmed. Here is the complete, proven adoption set.

---

## 1 · `overrides/app/theme/components/button.ts`

```diff
+// Icon-variant opacity levels. No foundation opacity token covers element-level opacity
+// (colors.opacity holds RGBA overlays, not multipliers), so named constants are the
+// correct pattern per conventions.md > "No magic numbers or strings."
+const OPACITY_ICON_HOVER    = 0.6;
+const OPACITY_ICON_DISABLED = 0.4;
+// 0.15s, matching baseStyle. Deliberately NOT var(--zimm-motion-duration-fast) (200ms):
+// see baseStyle's transition comment above — retiming needs UI-designer sign-off, and
+// motion.ts is itself marked provisional. One constant so icon/iconInverse cannot drift.
+const ICON_TRANSITION = 'opacity 0.15s ease';

 icon: {
-  transition: 'opacity 0.15s ease',
+  transition: ICON_TRANSITION,
-  _hover:    { opacity: 0.6 },
+  _hover:    { opacity: OPACITY_ICON_HOVER },
-  _disabled: { opacity: 0.4 },
+  _disabled: { opacity: OPACITY_ICON_DISABLED },
 },
 iconInverse: { … identical four lines … },
```

> **Proven:** theme output byte-identical for opacity. Jersey's token measured **0.2s** in-browser; this measured **0.15s**, matching baseline. The only line altered from theirs is `ICON_TRANSITION`.

---

## 2 · `overrides/app/types/contentful.ts` + `footer/index.tsx`

```diff
 export type FooterConfigEntry = {
   fields: {
     copyrightOwner?: string;
+    phoneHref?: string;
+    whatsAppHref?: string;
+    emailHref?: string;
   };
 };
```

```diff
-  const { subscribeHeading, subscribeBody, navGroups, legalLinks = [], copyrightOwner } = data.fields;
+  const { subscribeHeading, subscribeBody, navGroups, legalLinks = [], copyrightOwner, phoneHref, whatsAppHref, emailHref } =
+    data.fields;

-  <ContactIconRow />
+  <ContactIconRow phoneHref={phoneHref} whatsAppHref={whatsAppHref} emailHref={emailHref} />
```

> **Proven:** with values, renders three focusable `<a>` (`tel:`, `wa.me`, `mailto:`). With our empty fixture, Phase 3 stays **20/20** — zero risk today. ⚠️ With values it drops to **19/20**: our `contact icons are not focusable` assertion encodes the bug as correct and will need rewriting when Contentful lands.

---

## 3 · `scripts/generateRegistry.mjs` — hybrid

```diff
+ * When `preferredTypeName` is given (e.g. "FooterProps"), only that block's props
+ * are returned if it exists — prevents sub-component internal Props types in the
+ * same file from leaking into the registry row for the public component.
+ * Falls back to collecting all *Props blocks when the preferred name isn't found.
   */
-function extractTsProps(content, componentName) {
+function extractTsProps(content, preferredTypeName = null) {
   const re = /(?:type|interface)\s+(\w*Props)\s*(?:=\s*)?\{([\s\S]*?)\n\}/g
-  const blocks = []
+  const allBlocks = []
   let blockMatch
   while ((blockMatch = re.exec(content)) !== null) {
-    blocks.push({ name: blockMatch[1], body: blockMatch[2] })
-  }
-  const own = componentName && blocks.find((b) => b.name === `${componentName}Props`)
-  const selected = own ? [own] : blocks
-  const props = []
-  const seen = new Set()
-  for (const block of selected) {
-    const body = block.body
-    const lineRe = /^\s{2,}(\w+)(\??):\s*([^\n;,]+)[;,]?\s*$/gm
+    const typeName = blockMatch[1]
+    const body = blockMatch[2]
+    const blockProps = []
+    const blockSeen = new Set()
+    const lineRe = /^\s{2,}(\w+)(\??):\s*(.+?)\s*[;,]?\s*$/gm
     let m
     while ((m = lineRe.exec(body)) !== null) {
       const name = m[1]
-      if (seen.has(name) || name === 'children') continue
-      seen.add(name)
+      if (blockSeen.has(name) || name === 'children') continue
+      blockSeen.add(name)
       const optional = m[2] === '?'
-      const rawType = m[3].trim()
-      const type = rawType.length > 30 ? `${rawType.slice(0, 29)}…` : rawType
-      props.push(`${name}${optional ? '?' : ''}: ${type}`)
+      const type = m[3].trim()
+      blockProps.push(`${name}${optional ? '?' : ''}: ${type}`)
+    }
+    allBlocks.push({typeName, props: blockProps})
+  }
+
+  if (preferredTypeName) {
+    const preferred = allBlocks.find(({typeName}) => typeName === preferredTypeName)
+    if (preferred) return preferred.props
+  }
+
+  // Fallback: merge all blocks, deduplicating by prop name (first occurrence wins).
+  const seen = new Set()
+  const props = []
+  for (const {props: blockProps} of allBlocks) {
+    for (const p of blockProps) {
+      const name = p.split(/[?:]/)[0]
+      if (!seen.has(name)) { seen.add(name); props.push(p) }
     }
   }
   return props
 }

- extractTsProps(content, toPascalCase(folder))
+ extractTsProps(content, `${toPascalCase(folder)}Props`)

- extractTsProps(content, name)
+ extractTsProps(content, `${name}Props`)
```

**Keep unchanged from ours** — verified present in the hybrid: `escapeCell` (4 call sites, all three tables) and `const BASE_CACHE_SCHEMA = 3`.

> **Proven:** ours captured **4 of 6** probe props (comma types vanished entirely — the line never matched `$`); Jersey's captured 6 but left hooks/utils unescaped; hybrid gives 6/6 **and** escaping. **210 rows, 0 column mismatches.** Real delta: `ZimmNavItem`'s `React.MouseEvent<HTMLAnch…` → full `React.MouseEvent<HTMLAnchorElement \| HTMLButtonElement>`.
>
> Ready-to-use file: `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/KEEP-generateRegistry-hybrid.mjs`

---

## 4 · `zimmNavItem/index.stories.tsx`

```diff
 export const PlaceholderButton: Story = {
-  name: 'Placeholder — No href',
-  args: { label: 'Sale' },
+  name: 'Placeholder — No href (or unsafe href) renders as button',
+  render: () => (
+    <Box display="flex" flexDirection="column" gap={2} alignItems="flex-start">
+      <ZimmNavItem label="Omitted href" />
+      <ZimmNavItem label="javascript: href" href="javascript:void(0)" />
+      <ZimmNavItem label="data: href" href="data:text/html,xss" />
+      <ZimmNavItem label="Protocol-relative href" href="//example.com" />
+    </Box>
+  ),
+  play: async ({ canvasElement }) => {
+    const canvas = within(canvasElement);
+    // SAFE_HREF_RE rejects javascript:, data:, and protocol-relative // hrefs —
+    // each must fall back to <button> with no href attribute (not an <a>).
+    const cases = ['Omitted href', 'javascript: href', 'data: href', 'Protocol-relative href'];
+    for (const label of cases) {
+      const el = canvas.getByRole('button', { name: label });
+      await expect(el).toBeInTheDocument();
+      await expect(el).not.toHaveAttribute('href');
+    }
+  },
 };
```

> **Proven:** passes against our component. Mutation-caught — removing `(?!\/)` (the exact bypass `e9c2180` closed) **fails**; allowing `javascript:` **fails**. Control confirms safe hrefs still render `<a>`. No imports needed — ours already has `Box`, `expect`, `within`.

---

## 5 · `zimmInputAction/index.stories.tsx` — append

```diff
+export const EmptySubmitValidation: Story = {
+  name: 'Submit Validation — empty value',
+  args: { label: 'Email address', type: 'email', onSubmit: fn() },
+  play: async ({ canvasElement, args }) => {
+    const canvas = within(canvasElement);
+    await userEvent.click(canvas.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i }));
+    await expect(canvas.getByRole('alert')).toHaveTextContent(/please enter a value/i);
+    await expect(args.onSubmit).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
+  },
+};
+
+export const InvalidEmailValidation: Story = {
+  name: 'Submit Validation — invalid email format',
+  args: { label: 'Email address', type: 'email', onSubmit: fn() },
+  play: async ({ canvasElement, args }) => {
+    const canvas = within(canvasElement);
+    await userEvent.type(canvas.getByRole('textbox', { name: /email address/i }), 'not-an-email');
+    await userEvent.click(canvas.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i }));
+    await expect(canvas.getByRole('alert')).toHaveTextContent(/please enter a valid email address/i);
+    await expect(args.onSubmit).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
+  },
+};
```

> **Proven:** both assertions match our `VALIDATION_EMPTY` / `VALIDATION_EMAIL` strings and `buttonLabel = 'Submit'` default. Mutation-caught ×3 — dropping either guard **fails**, and so does the silent-submit case (guard fires but `onSubmit` still called). No imports needed — ours already has `fn`, `userEvent`.

---

## Not adopted

```diff
  # utils/cssVars.ts — keep our deletion (git rm on conflict)
  # locale button `disabled` — reverses your decision; Phase 3 stays green either way
```

## Integration result

All five applied together: `tsc` **0** · vitest **168/168** · prettier clean · Phase 3 **20/20** · transition **0.15s**.

