content.text:
Mobile changes the picture, and I should show you before doing anything else.

```
@1440   footer Δ5    (was Δ21)   ← site-map column absorbs most of it
@768    footer Δ0    (was Δ7)
@375    footer Δ22   (was Δ22)   ← columns stack, no neighbour to absorb
valid submit         Δ0 at both  ← earlier fix intact
```

The gap fix is a genuine conformance win on desktop and tablet. **It does nothing on mobile** — and it can't, because the design's anti-jump mechanism *is* the headroom under the site-map column, and when the columns stack there is no headroom.

**The design has the same characteristic.** Its subscribe section grows 126 → 143 on error. Side by side that's invisible; stacked, it moves everything below it. So Figma doesn't solve mobile either — a jump there is inherent to an in-flow error message.

Getting Δ0 on mobile requires *reserving* space, which is a deliberate deviation from the design rather than an implementation of it.

